<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕŏpompos</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θεόπομπος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek historian
				and orator</i>, <i>a pupil of Isocrates</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				de Or. 2, 13, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 23, 94</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 9,
			36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Alcib. 11, 1</span></i>. —
			Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕŏ-pompēus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-īnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Theopompus</i>, <i>Theopompean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Theopompino genere (dicendi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 6, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Theopompeo more,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Or. 61, 207</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
